Befunge-93 "Hello World" Program
==================================
Befunge is a two-dimensional esoteric programming language where the program counter
can move in four directions: right (>), left (<), up (^), and down (v).

Program:
--------
"dlroW olleH">:#,_@

Execution Flow:
---------------
1. Start at top-left (0,0), moving right by default
2. " enters string mode - characters are pushed to stack as ASCII values
3. "dlroW olleH" pushes "Hello World" in REVERSE (stack is LIFO)
4. " exits string mode
5. > sets direction to right (redundant but explicit)
6. : duplicates top of stack
7. # skips next instruction
8. , pops and outputs character as ASCII
9. _ is horizontal IF: pops value, goes right if 0, left if non-zero
   - If stack not empty (non-zero), goes LEFT back to ":"
   - If stack empty (zero), goes RIGHT to "@"
10. @ terminates program

The loop (:#,_) continues until all characters are printed.

Direction Commands:
> move right
< move left
^ move up
v move down

Key Commands Used:
" toggle string mode (push ASCII values)
: duplicate top of stack
# bridge (skip next instruction)
, pop and output as character
_ horizontal conditional (pop: if 0 go right, else left)
@ end program
